# speaking — a Speaking modus mentis puts conversation first
#
# Observing: Banter (Observation + Speaking) is asked to look at somebody in the Test Hall. A
# speaking mind never turns away from a person, so the declining --refuse-focus forces on any other
# observation is not open to it, and somebody is observed.
#
# Thinking: Rhetoric (Thinking + Speaking), thinking about that person, is offered only the
# conversations among their goals, and a conversation's means are narrowed to the one speaking
# action modus mentis held, Boasting — so the act is Boasting's and no attack is offered.
#
# Not reachable here: a speaking action modus mentis never refusing a conversation (the playground
# always answers "willing"), and never turning away from a person (the playground never turns away,
# and --refuse-focus deliberately wins over the rule).
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Hall" --period dawn --grant-mm banter,rhetoric,boasting,knack --refuse-focus

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
advance 12 180

# Banter is asked to look at somebody. A speaking mind does not turn away from a person: the
# declining --refuse-focus forces on every other observation is not open to it here.
click observe person
choose banter
advance 12 180
expect-state trees observer=banter
expect-no-state trees refusal

# Rhetoric thinks about them: of what a person affords it wants the conversation, and a speaking
# means carries that out — Boasting, not the Knack.
strategy succeed
click think last
choose rhetoric
advance 12 180
expect-state trees means=boasting
expect-no-state trees verb=attack
expect-no-state trees means=knack
quit
